@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "How 12 Week Recomp Works";
    ViewData["PublicPage"] = true;
}

<style>
    .how-page{max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.25rem 4rem;color:var(--text-color,#eef6ff)}
    .how-hero{text-align:center;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto 2rem}
    .how-kicker{font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#48d7ff;font-size:.85rem;margin:0 0 .7rem}
    .how-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,6vw,5.6rem);line-height:.94;margin:.15rem 0 .9rem;font-weight:950;letter-spacing:-.045em}
    .how-hero h1 span{color:#55e890}
    .how-hero p{font-size:clamp(1.05rem,2vw,1.35rem);line-height:1.6;opacity:.86;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto}
    .how-setup{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:1rem;align-items:center;padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:2rem auto 2.1rem;max-width:930px;border:1px solid rgba(81,217,255,.34);background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(30,102,164,.22),rgba(39,201,137,.10));border-radius:22px}
    .how-setup-icon{width:58px;height:58px;border-radius:18px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:rgba(65,208,255,.14);font-size:1.8rem}
    .how-setup strong{display:block;font-size:1.12rem;margin-bottom:.25rem}
    .how-setup span{opacity:.82;line-height:1.5}
    .how-steps{display:grid;gap:1rem;margin:0 auto 2.8rem;max-width:980px}
    .how-step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:72px 110px 1fr;gap:1.15rem;align-items:center;padding:1.2rem 1.25rem;border-radius:24px;border:1px solid rgba(116,178,229,.28);background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(17,48,83,.82),rgba(8,27,47,.92));box-shadow:0 18px 50px rgba(0,0,0,.16)}
    .how-number{width:58px;height:58px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:1.7rem;font-weight:950;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2cb9ff,#50e68b);color:#061626;box-shadow:0 0 28px rgba(61,211,218,.24)}
    .how-icon{width:100px;height:82px;border-radius:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);display:grid;place-items:center}
    .how-icon svg{width:64px;height:64px;stroke:#58dfff;fill:none;stroke-width:2.2;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}
    .how-step:nth-child(2) .how-icon svg{stroke:#65e19a}
    .how-step:nth-child(3) .how-icon svg{stroke:#b98cff}
    .how-copy h2{font-size:clamp(1.3rem,2.6vw,1.75rem);margin:0 0 .35rem}
    .how-copy p{margin:0;line-height:1.55;opacity:.84;font-size:1.03rem}
    .how-prescription{max-width:1040px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(1.4rem,4vw,2.4rem);border:1px solid rgba(81,232,144,.34);border-radius:28px;background:radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0,rgba(51,173,227,.16),transparent 45%),rgba(8,24,43,.88)}
    .how-prescription-header{text-align:center;max-width:820px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem}
    .how-prescription-header small{display:block;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#59e58f;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.45rem}
    .how-prescription-header h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.3rem);line-height:1;margin:.2rem 0 .8rem}
    .how-prescription-header p{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.62;opacity:.85;margin:0}
    .how-points{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.8rem;margin:1.25rem 0 1.8rem}
    .how-point{padding:1rem 1.05rem;border-radius:18px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.055);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08);line-height:1.5}
    .how-point strong{color:#74e6ff}
    .how-diagram{margin:1.7rem auto 0;background:#f8fcff;padding:.7rem;border-radius:22px;box-shadow:0 18px 60px rgba(0,0,0,.22)}
    .how-diagram img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:15px}
    .how-finish{max-width:850px;margin:2rem auto 0;text-align:center;padding:1.7rem 1.4rem;border-radius:24px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(43,187,255,.15),rgba(75,231,137,.12));border:1px solid rgba(84,213,255,.22)}
    .how-finish strong{display:block;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,2.8rem);margin-bottom:.5rem}
    .how-finish p{margin:.25rem auto;line-height:1.6;max-width:720px;opacity:.87}
    .how-actions{display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1.1rem}
    .how-actions a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:46px;padding:.75rem 1.15rem;border-radius:14px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:850}
    .how-actions .primary{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2ebcff,#4ee68a);color:#061522}
    .how-actions .secondary{border:1px solid rgba(127,211,255,.34);color:inherit;background:rgba(255,255,255,.05)}
    @@media(max-width:720px){.how-page{padding-top:2rem}.how-step{grid-template-columns:54px 76px 1fr;gap:.75rem;padding:1rem}.how-number{width:48px;height:48px;font-size:1.4rem}.how-icon{width:72px;height:66px}.how-icon svg{width:48px;height:48px}.how-points{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    @@media(max-width:520px){.how-step{grid-template-columns:48px 1fr}.how-icon{grid-column:2;width:100%;height:74px}.how-copy{grid-column:2}.how-setup{grid-template-columns:1fr;text-align:center}.how-setup-icon{margin:auto}}
</style>

<main class="how-page">
    <section class="how-hero">
        <p class="how-kicker">HOW 12 WEEK RECOMP WORKS</p>
        <h1>Set it up once.<br><span>Then just track.</span></h1>
        <p>
            Start with a basic weight and activity profile, tell 12WR how you prefer to move during the week,
            and the system builds the framework. After that, your daily job is remarkably simple.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="how-setup" aria-label="Initial setup">
        <div class="how-setup-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚙️</div>
        <div>
            <strong>First, give 12WR the basics.</strong>
            <span>Your starting body data, normal activity level, goal, and preferred weekly movement schedule give the engine the baseline it needs. You can change the schedule later. Once that is set, 12WR does the calculations.</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="how-steps" aria-label="Three daily steps">
        <article class="how-step">
            <div class="how-number">1</div>
            <div class="how-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><rect x="10" y="10" width="44" height="44" rx="9"/><path d="M22 25h20"/><path d="M32 25v9"/><path d="M26 19h12"/><path d="M21 44c4-4 18-4 22 0"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="how-copy">
                <h2>Morning weigh-in</h2>
                <p>Step on the scale and enter your weight in <strong>Recomp Tracking</strong>. If your scale gives body-fat, skeletal-muscle, water, waist, or visceral-fat data, add those too—but weight alone is enough to keep the daily trend moving.</p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="how-step">
            <div class="how-number">2</div>
            <div class="how-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><path d="M14 34h36c-1 11-8 17-18 17s-17-6-18-17Z"/><path d="M20 29c4-8 8-11 12-11 3 0 5 2 6 5 4-3 8-2 11 2"/><path d="M25 16c0 5-2 9-6 12"/><path d="M39 13c-1 5 0 9 4 12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="how-copy">
                <h2>Track what you eat</h2>
                <p>Use the <strong>Nutrition Logger</strong> during the day. 12WR cares most about where your protein, fat, and carbohydrate totals land. You do not have to eat perfectly “clean” all the time—the goal is to stay at or reasonably close to your prescribed macros.</p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <article class="how-step">
            <div class="how-number">3</div>
            <div class="how-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64"><path d="M22 24v16M42 24v16M16 27v10M48 27v10M10 30v4M54 30v4M22 32h20"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="how-copy">
                <h2>Enter your workout</h2>
                <p>Log the workout you actually did in the <strong>Workout Tracker</strong>. You do not need to beat yourself up or be sore every day. Challenge your muscles a few days each week—and more when your plan and recovery support it—then record what really happened.</p>
            </div>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section class="how-prescription">
        <div class="how-prescription-header">
            <small>YOUR DATA → YOUR PRESCRIPTION</small>
            <h2>12WR takes over from there.</h2>
            <p>
                The system combines your profile, preferred schedule, scale trend, nutrition, completed workouts,
                and recovery information to calculate your daily <strong>movement and macro prescription</strong>.
                The result is waiting on your Dashboard: what to do, how hard to do it, and the protein, fat,
                and carbohydrate targets that fit that day.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="how-points">
            <div class="how-point"><strong>You do not have to follow it perfectly.</strong> The closer you stay to the prescription, the more closely you are applying the science-based mechanics the program was designed around.</div>
            <div class="how-point"><strong>Macros matter more than perfection.</strong> An imperfect meal does not ruin the day. Track it, see where your totals are headed, and make the next choice fit.</div>
            <div class="how-point"><strong>Training should be productive, not punishing.</strong> Give your muscles a real reason to adapt several times each week, while letting recovery determine how much more is appropriate.</div>
            <div class="how-point"><strong>Track every day and watch the trend.</strong> If results begin to slip away from the direction you want, tighten things up a little. The system keeps recalculating from what you actually do.</div>
        </div>

        <figure class="how-diagram">
            <img src="/images/recomp/how-12wr-works-infographic.webp"
                 alt="12 Week Recomp prescription system showing scale tracking, workout tracking and nutrition tracking flowing into the prescription engine and back into a personalized daily movement and macro plan." />
        </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="how-finish">
        <strong>That’s really it.</strong>
        <p>
            12WR does the calculations. You move, track your food, record your workouts, and watch the results.
            Keep feeding the system real data and it keeps giving you a current plan instead of a generic population-average target.
        </p>
        <div class="how-actions">
            <a class="primary" href="/trial/start">Start Free</a>
            <a class="secondary" href="/GuidedDemo">See the Guided Demo</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
